      "head_commit": {
        "id": "f4f2e50adaf241f07d49ef88a14d0a6a83810d26",
        "tree_id": "cdd4872f454024aa91754c85602ea45f45702f05",
        "message": "docs: ISSUE-LOG — the iOS app builds, links, and its tests run\n\nRun 36671474326, both jobs green. Before this session nothing in ios/ had ever\nbeen compiled: canImport(GsFfi) was false, probe() returned libraryMissing, and\nthat is a supported configuration, so it read green.\n\nTwelve runs to get here, each failing at the next thing:\n\n    36659050115  hardcoded Xcode_16.2.app, not on the image\n    36660102564  slice check grepped a name that does not exist\n    36662206901  first compile: 4 pre-existing Swift bugs\n    36663379374  first link: 21 undefined libc++ symbols\n    36664200219  no x86_64 simulator slice; the runner was Intel\n    36665244922  x86_64-apple-ios-sim is not a Rust target\n    36666106903  the arch ARGUMENT was passed as a label\n    36667019000  ar cannot read a fat archive\n    36667890600  lipo -thin on a thin library is an error\n    36668750491  xcframework GREEN and uploaded\n    36669723190  app COMPILES AND LINKS; test bundle missing its import\n    36670596253  two methods throw XCTSkip without declaring throws\n    36671474326  ALL GREEN\n\nAll 7 GsNative tests executed for the first time:\n\n    passed  testFrameworkIsReachableOrAbsentCleanly          0.011s\n    passed  testShutdownIsIdempotent                         0.002s\n    skipped testChatReturnsNonEmptyText                      0.016s\n    skipped testEmbedImageRejectsShortBuffer                 0.211s\n    skipped testFailureThrowsRatherThanReturningEmptyString  0.004s\n    skipped testOcrReturnsTextOnFixture                      0.002s\n    skipped testSamePromptTwiceIsIdentical                   0.001s\n\nWhole AppTests bundle: 40 passed, 0 failed, 5 skipped.\n\nThe five skips had a cause, in the log:\n\n    GsNativeLoader: native engine unavailable: no GsFfi framework:\n      framework imported but no build info\n\nbuildInfo read gs_last_error() -- the FAILURE channel -- so it returned \"\" when\nno error was pending, which on a healthy engine is always. The framework was\nimported and linked; the engine reported itself missing. gs_mobile_build_info()\nis the function for that and it is in gs_mobile.h:95, one of the two headers the\nxcframework publishes. Fixed in 8fa8792, not yet proven by a run.\n\nWorth recording WHY a green job hid this: the two tests that could run without an\nengine both passed. A green job reporting an engine that reports itself missing\nis only visible because the gate prints the skip count instead of folding skips\ninto passes -- the same reason a2 and a6 were worth adding.",
